# What is known about particular cellular modules, as data.
#
# Decision 0043's shape: a quirk is a table entry somebody can read, diff and
# contribute without touching code, keyed on the USB id. A quirk expressed as a
# branch grows a second branch; a quirk expressed as a row does not.
#
# ## THIS TABLE EXPLAINS. IT DOES NOT DECIDE.
#
# The helpers behave correctly on a module that is not listed here, and that is
# a rule rather than an aspiration: `netcfgd-modem-at` waits for the module to
# dial and dials itself if it has not, which is right whether or not the module
# autoconnects. A table that *decided* would make every unlisted module behave
# worse -- and the unlisted module is the one somebody is holding when it
# fails.
#
# So what this is for is answering "why is this module like that", picking a
# sensible default port, and saying which helper applies at all.
#
# ## EVERY ROW IS MEASURED, AND SAYS ON WHAT
#
# A row nobody has run is a guess with a citation, which is worse than an empty
# table -- somebody will trust it. If you add one, add it from a module you
# have in front of you, and say what you read it off.
#
# ## FORMAT
#
#   vid:pid  key=value key=value ...
#
#   data=       ecm | mbim | qmi | rndis  -- the data path the firmware offers
#   helper=     at | mbim                 -- which helper can drive it
#   at=         N                         -- ttyUSB index that answers AT and
#                                            that a modem manager does not hold
#   autoconnect=yes | no                  -- the module dials its own context
#                                            on registration
#   note=       free text, no spaces around `=`
#
# `data=ecm` with `helper=mbim` would be a contradiction: a module offering only
# ECM presents no /dev/cdc-wdm for mbimcli to open, which is the whole reason
# the AT helper exists.

# Quectel EG916Q-GL. Measured 2026-07-28 and after, on an i.MX93 board with the
# module on a daughtercard: `+QCFG: "usbnet",1` (ECM; the firmware offers only
# 1 and 3, so no MBIM and no QMI exist to select), `+QCFG: "qcautoconnect",1`,
# `+QCFG: "nat",0`. Composition is four `option` ports plus `cdc_ether`.
#
# `at=3` because a running ModemManager held `ttyUSB2` and left `ttyUSB0`,
# `ttyUSB1` and `ttyUSB3` free -- checked by looking at what had the ports open
# rather than assumed from the port order. On a machine with no modem manager,
# 2 answers as well.
#
# `nat=0` is why the host takes a DHCP lease: the module bridges the operator's
# address rather than handing out a private one, so the ECM interface gets the
# real address and `config = "dhcp"` is all netcfgd needs.
2c7c:6007  data=ecm helper=at at=3 autoconnect=yes note=EG916Q-GL,firmware_EG916QGLLGR01A05M04
